)\n\ntsne_df = pd.DataFrame(tsne_coords, columns=[\"Dim1\", \"Dim2\"])\ntsne_df[[\"KMeans\", \"DBSCAN\", \"GMM\"]] = pd.DataFrame(\n    {\"KMeans\": kmeans_labels, \"DBSCAN\": dbscan_labels, \"GMM\": gmm_labels}\n)","metadata":{"id":"tsne_transform_cell","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-02-23T06:46:00.760825Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-02-23T06:46:00.761064Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-02-23T06:46:01.317700Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-02-23T06:46:00.761043Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-02-23T06:46:01.316956Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/sklearn/manifold/_t_sne.py:1164: FutureWarning: 'n_iter' was renamed to 'max_iter' in version 1.5 and will be removed in 1.7.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":20},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## t-SNE 2D Projection\n\nt-SNE was applied to project the high-dimensional data into **two nonlinear components (Dim1 and Dim2)**.  \nUnlike PCA, t-SNE focuses on preserving local neighborhood structure.  \nCluster labels from **KMeans**, **DBSCAN**, and **GMM** are visualized in the reduced space.  \nThis projection helps reveal hidden patterns and potential nonlinear separations.  \nThe visualization provides a more detailed view of cluster compactness and overlap.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\nfig.suptitle(\"t-SNE 2-D Projection – Cluster Assignments\", fontsize=14, y=1.01)\n\nfor ax, col, title in zip(axes, [\"KMeans\", \"DBSCAN\", \"GMM\"],\n                                  [\"K-Means\", \"DBSCAN\", \"Gaussian Mixture\"]):\n    sns.scatterplot(data=tsne_df, x=\"Dim1\", y=\"Dim2\",\n                    hue=col, palette=PALETTE, s=DOT_SIZE,\n                    edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.3, ax=ax)\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=12)\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"t-SNE Dimension 1\", fontsize=9)\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"t-SNE Dimension 2\", fontsize=9)\n    ax.legend